# Step by step nav

Number steps only when the order is necessary, and never mark one done because someone opened it. Step navigation connects a journey. It does not track completion. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Use it for a documented setup journey with a real beginning and end, such as understand requirements, install, then verify. Keep optional or unordered chores in a task list. Opening a guidance step does not mean it has been completed ([WG-035](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-035)).

## Structure and behaviour

Number the ordered stages and keep their action links visible ([WG-050](../../content/writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html#wg-050)). Explain prerequisites and optional branches in text. If disclosure controls shorten a long overview, the same headings and links must work without JavaScript. Each destination must stand alone for a direct visitor.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not store progress through this reference journey. Do not reuse the step design as an automation status display or to claim an installation succeeded. A service that needs saved completion belongs in an explicit task-list implementation.

